\ Two image modules export `probe`. The entry imports module B's, and module
\ A hands out a parameter default and a stored quotation -- both interpreted
\ at runtime inside the image -- that call A's own `probe`. The load-time
\ stamp must make them resolve A's deterministically instead of scanning the
\ module cache by name.

use { a-param: a-quot: } "fixtures/own_module_image_a.1z" ;
use { probe: } "fixtures/own_module_image_b.1z" ;

probe print-line
a-param get print-line
a-quot call print-line
